PAGE RESENDS
TITLE Resends: missing parts other stations asked for
KIND screen
SCREENS RESENDS
HELP Enter open  s send  d drop  A send all  ? guide
SEE FORM-PARTS_ASK FORM-PARTS_QUEUE FORM-PARTS_REPEAT EMCON MSG-VIEW
KEY Enter Opens the tape or bundle the row is about.
KEY s Sends the parts this row asked for, now or at the next net slot (asks first, No by default).
KEY d Drops the row: those parts won't be resent (asks first).
KEY A Sends everything that can go, after showing how many sends and how much room is left this hour (press y).
BEGIN_TEXT
Long key tapes and bundles go in numbered parts. A member missing some
asks for them by number (PARTS_ASK). Each ask is a row here.

Asks pool. A part several members missed goes once, to the whole net; a
part one member missed goes to that member. So one send can answer many
rows: after it goes, every row that asked for those parts shows SENT.

WAIT can go now. HELD-EMCON waits for EMCON to lift. HELD-CAP waits for
room: at most 12 resends go in an hour. HELD-NET is sent, held for the net
slot. FLAGGED: the member asked again for a part already sent twice. Look
into their antenna or path, then send it with s if you choose, or drop it.
END
BEGIN_EXAMPLE
Twenty members ask for parts of last night's tape and bundle. The rows
pool into 7 sends. Press A: "7 sends, room 12 this hour. Send? y".
END
